{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And whoever touches anything that was under him.</b> Of the zav — it comes and teaches about the riding-beast, that one who touches it is impure and does not require washing of garments. And this is a stringency in the bed over the riding-beast." "<b>And whoever carries them.</b> All that is stated in the matter of the zav — his flux, his spittle, his semen, his urine, and the bed and the riding-beast — carrying them imparts impurity to a person to impure garments (cf. Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:35.629993179Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}